arguments.content:
💡 **SUGGESTION: `Duration(milliseconds: ms)` can overflow into a garbage window — clamp the accepted range**

`int.tryParse` accepts anything that fits in 64 bits, so `FA_SIGINT_WINDOW_MS=9223372036854775807` parses fine — and `Duration(milliseconds: ms)` then multiplies by 1000 in microsecond space, silently wrapping into a **negative/garbage** duration on the VM. With a wrapped-negative `window`, `current.elapsed <= window` is never true, so every press silently becomes a fresh press 1 and the double-press exit stops working — exactly the "invalid value" class the doc comment promises is handled ("Invalid values are ignored silently (null), never errors").

```dart
Duration? resolveSigintWindowOverride({required Map<String, String> env}) {
  final ms = int.tryParse(env[kSigintWindowEnvVar]?.trim() ?? '');
  if (ms == null || ms <= 0 || ms > 60000) return null; // sane clamp
  return Duration(milliseconds: ms);
}
```

A one-sided clamp (anything above a minute is nonsense for this seam) makes the null-fallback promise true for every input. While there, the whitespace case the `trim()` exists for (`' 750 '`) is currently unpinned — one extra `expect(resolve(const {'FA_SIGINT_WINDOW_MS': ' 750 '}), const Duration(milliseconds: 750));` in the boundary test would lock it.

Severity: 💡 suggestion only — the seam is test-only and CI sets `12000`; nothing shipped regresses.

💡 **SUGGESTION: ACX.3 re-spells `spawnTui()`'s arguments instead of parameterizing the helper**

This spawn block duplicates the group's `spawnTui()` helper verbatim (`'HOME': tempHome.path`, `columns: 120`, `raw: false` + the same kernel-termios comment) and adds only `kSigintWindowEnvVar`:

```dart
final harness = await FaCliHarness.spawn(
  extraEnv: {
    'HOME': tempHome.path,
    kSigintWindowEnvVar: '${testWindow.inMilliseconds}',
  },
  columns: 120,
  raw: false, // kernel default termios: ISIG on, 0x03 delivers SIGINT
);
```

If the TUI spawn contract changes later (a new base arg added to the helper, a different geometry), ACX.3 silently drifts from its siblings. Passing extra env through the helper removes the copy:

```dart
Future<FaCliHarness> spawnTui({
  Map<String, String>? extraEnv,
}) => FaCliHarness.spawn(
  extraEnv: {'HOME': tempHome.path, ...?extraEnv},
  columns: 120,
  // Kernel default termios: ISIG on, 0x03 delivers SIGINT.
  raw: false,
);
```

Then ACX.3 becomes `await spawnTui(extraEnv: {kSigintWindowEnvVar: '${testWindow.inMilliseconds}'})`.

Severity: 💡 suggestion only — behavior is identical today.

